<title>UK: EIB sets 400 million Danish crown step-up bond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 400 million Danish crown step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager KreditEbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    400 MLN DKR   COUPON    *5.0	 MATURITY    07.APR.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  101.90    PAY DATE    07.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     LISTING    LUX	 YIELD AT I/P 5.59 PCT</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) 10	  YIELD AT F/F 5.88 PCT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC   1.25</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED DANISH GOVTS DUE 15.DEC.04</p>
<p>			    AND 15.AUG.05.</p>
<p> NOTES     FOR YEARS ONE TO FOUR THEN STEPS UP 7 PCT THEREAFTER.</p>
<p>	     ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
